Z||000000||Philphine||04-30-2001||04:19 PM||||has this happened to anyone? i just put a gt rear facia on my '87 coupe and will change from the single round tips i was using to some big duals i got. i'm just wondering how careful i might have to be when i mount them since they are wider across than that plate that is on the facia. i had 5" inch tips (shuddap...i liked them) with the coupe that sat pretty close to the facia (cut out other side 'cause i have a gt exhaust) and had no problems but i want to cover any bases i might need to.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-30-2001||06:19 PM||||just make sure you leave a space for the heat to disipate. dont let it touch any part of the facia. an inch or larger gap should be plenty. Ive seen some people make a shield out of aluminum or stainless steel to fit into the notch around the tips.||||reg||1
